  "method": "Native Bend-generated C and native Go fastssz on the same raw fixture bytes: read -> full typed decode (forced by a checksum fold inside the measured window) -> hash_tree_root -> serialize -> write, one sequential thread, fresh process per sample, three alternating samples per fixture. Every phase boundary is also an exit point, so each phase is measured by a separate process that stops there and whose peak resident size the kernel reports through wait4 ru_maxrss; decode_overhead_bytes is the decode-prefix kernel peak minus the input-prefix kernel peak, cross-checked against continuous sampling and the idle boundary readings and taking the maximum of all three. roundtrip_peak_rss_bytes is the whole-process kernel peak INCLUDING startup, the input representation, hashing, serialization and output, and is NOT the decode peak. Compilation excluded and always rebuilt. Output bytes compared exactly and `verified` derived from that comparison. No forced GC, no RSS subtraction beyond the documented bracketing run.",
